====================================================================================================
LEGALITY
====================================================================================================
  L1 EOM (phi):  -c*L_M(x)*Subs(Derivative(F(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, -c*phi(x) + 3*Derivative(phi(x), x)**2) + nu + 6*(c - 6*Derivative(phi(x), (x, 2)))*L_M(x)*Derivative(phi(x), x)**2*Subs(Derivative(F(_xi_1), (_xi_1, 2)), _xi_1, -c*phi(x) + 3*Derivative(phi(x), x)**2) - 6*L_M(x)*Derivative(phi(x), (x, 2))*Subs(Derivative(F(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, -c*phi(x) + 3*Derivative(phi(x), x)**2) - 6*Derivative(L_M(x), x)*Derivative(phi(x), x)*Subs(Derivative(F(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, -c*phi(x) + 3*Derivative(phi(x), x)**2) + Derivative(mu(x), (x, 2)) = 0
  L1 EOM (mu):   rhobar - rho(x) + Derivative(phi(x), (x, 2)) = 0
  [PASS] L1 EOM derivable: Euler-Lagrange for phi, mu (sympy)
  [PASS] L2 leaf scalar densities (CFG329 method): mu lap_h Phi_d, nu Phi_d, |D Phi_d|_h^2, <rho>_Sigma (as CFG329's <K>): scalars under leaf diffeos; H(s) of a scalar
  L3: no d_t of Phi_d, mu, nu appears -> no momenta; mu solved by an elliptic adjoint, nu by one global equation.
      On shell the constraint term vanishes; no conjugate grows (contrast CFG349's lambda = C/(1-m)).
  L4 adjoint vs finite difference: max rel err 2.3e-08; translation Noether sum (rel) 5.4e-12
